#
# Counter-example for math:IncompleteSheafSection: a math:LocalSection that names its
# math:sectionRegion but declares NO math:overSheaf — so it is anchored to no
# math:CellularSheaf and therefore to no actual stalk/restriction semantics. Local
# disagreement asserted over no declared stalk/restriction data is not a section at
# all. The math:LocalSection frame's qualified min-count on math:overSheaf fails, so
# validation MUST emit shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent (and no other
# finding): the region is present, isolating the missing sheaf anchor.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/gluing/> .

ex:region a math:CellComplex .

# A local section with a region but no carrier sheaf — no stalk/restriction semantics.
ex:orphanSection a math:LocalSection ;
    math:sectionRegion ex:region .
